00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.280
Because I think there's not this...

242
00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:30.600
When I look at these teams, I don't see a villain origin story or necessarily an underdog mentality.

243
00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:35.520
Like, these are teams that have the best players, have worked hard,

244
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:43.120
and have the feel-good stories mixed in with the program history as well to carry it on.

245
00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:43.900
All of...

246
00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:48.160
These are big-time programs with big-time names when you think about it.

247
00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:54.000
But it's still been so long between UConn, UCLA, and Texas.

248
00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.460
And then South Carolina's like, hey, don't forget about us.

249
00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:01.460
We're the new kids on the block in this dynasty type of thing.

250
00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:05.640
But we want to be here, and we also have some things to talk about.

251
00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:13.920
So, when we think back, when we think back to the 2024-25 season,

252
00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:22.340
what do you think will be that defining factor that would have defined this college basketball season?

253
00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.560
Ooh, that's a really great question.

254
00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.480
Right?

255
00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:26.320
No, that's deep.

256
00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:27.180
Shout out to our producer.

257
00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:27.680
That's deep.

258
00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:33.520
Honestly, you know, we think about the viewership in that 2024 WNBA draft class

259
00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:38.320
with Kaitlyn Clark, Angel Rees, Rekia Jackson, Cameron Brink, Camila Cardoso, Kate Martin.

260
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.820
I can go on and on and on.

261
00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.180
And it didn't stop.

262
00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:48.280
So, if I would put into a couple of words or maybe define it in one word,

263
00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:56.520
it's like continuation, like a season of continuation and no sign still of slowing down because there's more.

264
00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:03.540
We're still talking about Paige Beckers, Olivia Miles, Hannah Hidalgo, Madison Booker, Juju Watkins.

265
00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:08.600
Like, the talent is endless in women's basketball is here.

266
00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.700
It is here to stay.

267
00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.260
And it's exciting.

268
00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.000
Like, people are so excited.

269
00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:17.980
I have, you know, my friends texting me, calling me, telling me about the games.

270
00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.480
I'm like, okay, y'all are locked in.

271
00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.080
And these are casual fans.

272
00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.220
You don't have to be locked in.

273
00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:23.620
You don't have to be a diehard.

274
00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.980
It's people who are truly invested in what's going on.

275
00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:30.120
And it's so exciting.

276
00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.000
It's so refreshing.

277
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.040
And they deserve that.

278
00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.440
Like, we talked all season long about Unrivaled.

279
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.960
We talked about the W.

280
00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:42.380
We talked about these professional athletes who are performing at the highest level.

281
00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:46.660
And thank God people are finally waking up, you know?

282
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.940
So, it's been really cool.

283
00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:49.460
About time, Autumn.

284
00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.200
You can say it.

285
00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:50.780
About time.

286
00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:51.500
I'll say it.

287
00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:57.280
But also, for the newness, I love—I was going to say the exact same thing.

288
00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.620
I love everything that you said.

289
00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:04.200
And especially because you can follow this path of this new fan.

290
00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:08.540
You can—maybe Caitlin Clark was that name that brought you in.

291
00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:13.580
And you came in during the end of her college season last year.

292
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.720
And then you watched her Final Four.

293
00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.080
But then you got to watch South Carolina.

294
00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.440
You got to watch LSU.

295
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:20.820
You got to watch NC State.

296
00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.220
So, you were introduced to all of those prograMs.

297
00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:24.380
And you're like, oh, dang.

298
00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:24.720
Okay.

299
00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.420
Who are these?

300
00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:26.260
They balling out.

301
00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.400
Then you watch the championship game.

302
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.240
And you're hooked.

303
00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.320
And you're like, oh, my gosh.

304
00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:31.220
I can't wait.

305
00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:31.900
Wait.

306
00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:32.760
I don't have to wait.

307
00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.960
I just wait a couple weeks.

308
00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.680
And then the WNBA season starts.

309
00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:42.820
Like, you can see this through line of the fandom and how maybe it started last year.

310
00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.940
But you are definitely coming back.

311
00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:50.660
And maybe you bought tickets to Tampa because you're so excited from last season.

312
00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:53.180
So, that has been my favorite part.

313
00:15:53.360 --> 00:16:00.400
And I definitely think that people maybe were, maybe the doubters were expecting a huge drop-off.

314
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.000
But there was not a drop-off.

315
00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:07.000
And that is so exciting to me that it's continuing to build.

316
00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.500
That we have been seeing all the commercials.

317
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:10.020
Yes.

318
00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:11.240
All the opportunities.

319
00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.520
All the investments.

320
00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:17.620
Like, I loved, we were watching the ESPN halftime report.

321
00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.300
Some rounds, it was sponsored by Degree.

322
00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.460
And then it turns into a new sponsor.

323
00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:24.840
It's sponsored by Shea Moisture.

324
00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:29.300
Me and my husband were like, okay, we're doing, you know, ads by rounds now.

325
00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:34.340
Like, before, there was no sponsors for the women's events and the Women's March Madness.

326
00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:38.280
So, there is this overwhelming sense of investment.

327
00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.720
And it has not slowed down.

328
00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.440
If anything, it's picking up more steam.

329
00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:52.400
And when we get to the Final Four and the biggest stage, again, I'll say it, the basketball is super good and exciting.

330
00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.440
And the stars are starring.

331
00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.920
And then we have the eyeballs to go with it.

332
00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:02.740
So, that's just what gets me super excited heading into this Final Four.

333
00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.440
But enough of the big picture.

334
00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.180
We're going to get down to the teaMs.

335
00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:08.860
Let's pay some bills real quick, but we'll be right back.

336
00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.460
Welcome back to the Women's Hoop Show.

337
00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:29.500
And before we get to our Final Four preview, let's, let's, how did we get here?

338
00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:33.540
For each of these teams, how did they earn this spot?

339
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:37.540
Let's give a little recap of how they got here.

340
00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:42.000
And let's start with UCLA against LSU.

341
00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.820
That was their Elite Eight matchup.

342
00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:48.100
This was a rematch from last season.

343
00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.460
UCLA lost to LSU.

344
00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.660
And it was a winnable game last year.

345
00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.640
So, I know they had been thinking about this all year long.

346
00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:02.540
There was also some drama around this last year.

347
00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:10.360
Maybe you remember about the LA Times article that came out and really pitted the two teams

348
00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:16.460
against each other, essentially saying that one team was better than the other because

349
00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:20.940
of, I don't know, overall vibe, I guess you could say, Autumn.

350
00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:26.420
It was a poorly written opinion article that the writer has since apologized for.

351
00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:31.520
But that's all to say, there's some extra animosity heading into this game.

352
00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:35.160
And Flaje Johnson wanted all the smoke and she wanted it.

353
00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:42.800
But UCLA was able to win it 72 to 65 over an LSU team that was coming back.

354
00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:49.900
But what did you kind of see in this game to get UCLA over the hump of LSU?

355
00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:55.240
Yeah, well, just looking at UCLA, like in the region they played in, you looked at it and said,

356
00:18:55.240 --> 00:19:00.560
okay, no one can match up with Lauren Betts at 6'7 and the skill that she possesses.

357
00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.680
But LSU truly challenged them.

358
00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:05.120
I mean, Flaje Johnson coming out with 28 points.

359
00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.200
Anissa Morrow having that main challenge down low.

360
00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.120
It didn't matter.

361
00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:13.600
Like, she pulled the ball out, was knocking threes down, was knocking 10-footers,

362
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.320
no matter what, getting in transition, banging down low.

363
00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:21.120
Anissa Morrow is going to go down as one of the greatest we have seen in this game.

364
00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:25.420
And she said it herself, like, no one has done what I've done in my college career.

365
00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.400
Missed double-double with 104 double-doubles overall.

366
00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.460
That's insane to say.

367
00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:32.560
Like, what?

368
00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.060
104 is crazy.

369
00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:38.000
And she's consistently leading the nations in double-doubles.

370
00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:44.320
So I had no questions or concerns going ahead, going up against Lauren Betts or just anyone

371
00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.940
in the paint, how she alters shots at 6'7".

372
00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:50.680
It didn't bluster or bother Anissa whatsoever.

373
00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:56.360
But the thing about it, when we look at UCLA, we always talk about Lauren Betts.

374
00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.380
But here's the Bruins saying, hello, there's more.

375
00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:05.160
And I think this tournament alone is showcasing the balance that UCLA has.

376
00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.700
This has been all season long.

377
00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:09.940
This isn't just a coming-out party for Gabriela Hawkins.

378
00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.160
She is the unsung hero of this team.

379
00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.720
And if you have been watching them closely, she's had games like this.

380
00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:17.800
She's had timely moments like this.

381
00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.540
18 points to lead her team.

382
00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:21.880
Four for five from deep.

383
00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.180
Those were game-changing threes.

384
00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.180
And she also did it on both ends.

385
00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:33.140
She had to guard Laje Johnson, Michaela Williams, like two of the best guards we have seen in

386
00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.060
this game as well.

387
00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.400
That's not an easy feat whatsoever.

388
00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:38.740
And she does it on both ends.

389
00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.780
She still has the energy to knock down those big shots.

390
00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:45.080
But you also had Tania Gartner coming off the bench.

391
00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.240
15 points.

392
00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:51.640
You're talking about pieces you've got in the transfer portal that are now coming into play.

393
00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.900
And she's been able to break out as well throughout the course of the season.

394
00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.540
But in a timely manner, 15 points, including five threes.

395
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.380
That was a difference maker.

396
00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.480
I think the balance has been that all season long.

397
00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.960
And it's definitely going to help as they try to pursue a championship.

398
00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:06.740
Absolutely.

399
00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.740
41% from the three-point line for UCLA.

400
00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:15.700
And when they're knocking those down and having Lauren Betts inside, what do you choose?

401
00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:16.320
I don't know.

402
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:16.550
Make your poison.

403
00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:17.300
Good luck.

404
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:25.840
Kim Mulkey, the head coach of LSU, said that that game was won or lost in the second quarter.

405
00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:31.380
And to put it in perspective, Lauren Betts gets two fouls early.

406
00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:34.740
Which, by the way, she has never done before.

407
00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:39.780
This was her first DMP in a quarter of her career.

408
00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:42.900
She did not play the entire second quarter.

409
00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:48.540
And, you know, for this other show that I'm doing on Locked On Women's Basketball,

410
00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:53.740
we talked about kind of the difference between her and Cameron Brink as a post player and how

411
00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:56.740
Cameron Brink at Stanford, that was her detriment.

412
00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:58.100
She would get in foul trouble.

413
00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:03.620
And Stanford had to, like, really know how to play without her because it happens so often.

414
00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:06.220
Lauren Betts does not foul.

415
00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:09.380
She is so smart and has body control.

416
00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:13.460
And as a shot blocker at 6'7", that is really hard to do.

417
00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:19.920
But she sits out the entire second quarter and everyone's like, uh-oh, this is where LSU is

418
00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:20.700
going to turn up.

419
00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:24.000
No, that's where Tamia Gardner makes three threes.

420
00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:26.620
That's where Gabrielle Jaquez has five points.

421
00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.160
Kiki has two points.

422
00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:33.540
And it's like, oh, they have other people that can show up.

423
00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:39.140
And LSU did not take advantage of those minutes when Betts were not on the floor.

424
00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:41.240
And that's what the coach said.

425
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.500
It didn't even matter what happened in the third quarter.

426
00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:45.160
It didn't matter what happened in the fourth quarter.

427
00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:51.620
They did not take advantage and go on a run and force Corey Close to put Lauren Betts back in.

428
00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:53.620
And that was a huge difference maker.

429
00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:54.120
Would you agree?

430
00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:54.640
I would agree.

431
00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:58.180
I mean, 22-6 in that second quarter.

432
00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:01.820
Would you have pictured that without Lauren Betts, Jordan?

433
00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:08.920
Like, to me, that says a lot about the Bruins.

434
00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:13.220
And they are not peaking at the right time, but they're just playing their best basketball

435
00:23:13.220 --> 00:23:14.580
at the right time.

436
00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:19.100
And their teammates are stepping up in the moments that are needed the moSt.

437
00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:23.180
And even before that, Lauren Betts had a 30-10 game.

438
00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:26.960
Like, she's coming in and she's not being denied of this moment.

439
00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:29.780
We saw that in the Big Ten Championship game, too.

440
00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.020
Willing her team to a win that want to.

441
00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.500
And you have all the pieces.

442
00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:38.480
I think this year, compared to last year, they have the experience.

443
00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:39.460
They have the pieces.

444
00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:40.300
They have the depth.

445
00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:41.120
They have the balance.

446
00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.720
Now it's like that extra, like, grit to them.

447
00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:51.980
You know, like, that extra, like, confidence, that swag, that, that just want to overall.

448
00:23:52.300 --> 00:23:54.100
That I will not be denied.

449
00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:57.800
And I think that is what separates you from other teaMs.

450
00:23:58.380 --> 00:23:59.600
Yeah, for sure.

451
00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:02.940
Well, LSU, they're going to try to figure it out.

452
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:08.200
The one stat that really stuck out to me was coming into this Elite Eight game against UCLA.

453
00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:12.900
LSU was 16-0 when Flauget scored over 20 points.

454
00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:14.460
And she dropped 28.

455
00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:16.000
She played amazing.

456
00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:17.420
She's only a sophomore.

457
00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:21.500
She is eligible to go into the WNBA draft.

458
00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:24.600
But my guess is that she's going to come back.

459
00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:28.140
Because I think there's other parts of her game that she can continue to grow.

460
00:24:28.520 --> 00:24:33.800
I also, I think a part of these guesses are, I think she's coming back to LSU.

461
00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:35.000
But we'll see.

462
00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:35.580
We'll see.

463
00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:36.560
I don't know anything.

464
00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:37.740
Who knows?

465
00:24:38.260 --> 00:24:39.800
But Flauget, she balled out.

466
00:24:39.980 --> 00:24:41.520
We know what she's going to do with LSU.

467
00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:44.140
Let's move on to the next number one team.

468
00:24:44.520 --> 00:24:45.960
Who's in the Final Four.

469
00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:50.360
South Carolina versus Duke in that Elite Eight game.

470
00:24:50.840 --> 00:24:52.440
Oh, my goodness.

471
00:24:52.860 --> 00:24:54.900
This was such a good game.

472
00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:58.220
It was a very low-scoring affair.

473
00:24:58.620 --> 00:25:00.540
54-50.

474
00:25:01.060 --> 00:25:04.940
South Carolina barely hangs on to win that game.

475
00:25:04.940 --> 00:25:08.220
Which we talked about the last game being in the second quarter.

476
00:25:08.440 --> 00:25:12.320
This game was won or lost in like the last two minutes, I would say.

477
00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:14.220
Duke had all the momentum.

478
00:25:14.500 --> 00:25:18.740
Kind of fell apart with a few decision makings towards the end there.

479
00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:21.920
And to me, Autumn, this was experience.

480
00:25:22.400 --> 00:25:25.800
This was experience over don't panic, don't panic.

481
00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:26.860
Oh, we panicked.

482
00:25:26.860 --> 00:25:30.380
That's how I felt Duke kind of looked towards the end there.

483
00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:35.020
But South Carolina did not play their best against Maryland.

484
00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:36.240
Barely won that one.

485
00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:39.360
Then they come in and they barely win against Duke.

486
00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:44.500
I don't think we expected this type of performance this late.

487
00:25:44.580 --> 00:25:44.680
Yeah.

488
00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:50.680
Especially when we see other teams who are, you know, blown out by 20 or more points.

489
00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:52.340
That's what South Carolina used to do.

490
00:25:52.620 --> 00:25:54.980
But now these are a little close.

491
00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:56.600
And I was a little nervous.

492
00:25:56.880 --> 00:25:57.520
Were you a little nervous?

493
00:25:57.520 --> 00:25:58.440
I was definitely nervous.

494
00:25:58.620 --> 00:25:59.800
I was screaming at the TV.

495
00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:03.660
And honestly, Jordan, I think we're all spoiled at this point.

496
00:26:03.880 --> 00:26:08.080
Because we are used to seeing South Carolina dominate.

497
00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:11.920
And I want to read you something because I thought this was very interesting.

498
00:26:11.920 --> 00:26:20.280
During last year's run to the Final Four, South Carolina trailed for a total of one minute and 10 seconds.

499
00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:23.840
One minute and 10 seconds.

500
00:26:24.080 --> 00:26:30.660
This year, the Gamecocks were behind for a total of 36 minutes and 27 seconds.

501
00:26:30.880 --> 00:26:32.560
Which was still really good.

502
00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:33.500
It's still a low number.

503
00:26:33.700 --> 00:26:39.340
But one minute, like South Carolina was blowing through teams, flying colors.

504
00:26:40.240 --> 00:26:42.540
Throughout this whole championship pursuit.

505
00:26:42.760 --> 00:26:44.060
And now we're so used to that.

506
00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:45.080
So accustomed to it.

507
00:26:45.220 --> 00:26:46.160
It's like, whoa, hold on now.

508
00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:48.020
Like, these are some tight games.

509
00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:52.800
And we haven't had to hold our breath like this for a minute for South Carolina.

510
00:26:53.040 --> 00:27:00.020
So when I looked at that game, Duke had plenty of opportunity to make it happen and shake the world.

511
00:27:00.260 --> 00:27:03.040
But like you said, that experience really played through.

512
00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:03.760
Like, they've been here.

513
00:27:03.840 --> 00:27:05.100
We talked about this last episode.

514
00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:06.600
They've been here before.

515
00:27:06.600 --> 00:27:12.780
A lot of these players, I think it's like eight players overall on this current roster, were here last year.

516
00:27:12.980 --> 00:27:14.400
And then they bring on some new pieces.

517
00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:15.700
They have that bench.

518
00:27:15.920 --> 00:27:18.920
For me, it has been the bench in these close stretches.

519
00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:22.940
In the first round, we saw a record-breaking 66 points.

520
00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:25.260
Indiana, it was 19 points.

521
00:27:25.400 --> 00:27:27.160
That was a really close nail-biter.

522
00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:28.880
Maryland was 40 points.

523
00:27:28.940 --> 00:27:31.260
But in that Duke game, guess how many bench points?

524
00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:33.420
How many?

525
00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:33.780
Nine.

526
00:27:35.100 --> 00:27:36.260
Oh, my gosh.

527
00:27:36.720 --> 00:27:40.240
This is a team that leads the nation in bench points.

528
00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:42.100
It's about 40 on the regular season.

529
00:27:42.300 --> 00:27:45.480
33 coming off the bench during this NCAA tournament run.

530
00:27:45.700 --> 00:27:47.020
Around that average.

531
00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:50.320
But nine points coming off the bench versus Duke.

532
00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:51.120
Whoa.

533
00:27:51.440 --> 00:27:53.800
That is such a good stat.

534
00:27:54.160 --> 00:27:58.040
Moesha Fawaii is that main person that is coming off the bench.

535
00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:00.620
Joyce Edwards, Tessa Johnson, all single digits.

536
00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:01.340
Yeah.

537
00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:02.540
Wow.

538
00:28:03.100 --> 00:28:06.260
And they still manage to get the win.

539
00:28:06.420 --> 00:28:10.340
And so I think it says a lot about that.

540
00:28:10.340 --> 00:28:14.800
I will say, and this may come off a little harsh, but I'm okay.

541
00:28:14.960 --> 00:28:15.600
I can take it.

542
00:28:16.600 --> 00:28:21.060
We talk a lot about how you don't want to bet against Dawn Staley.

543
00:28:21.620 --> 00:28:24.460
And you can't bet against Dawn Staley.

544
00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:30.820
But at the end of the day, Dawn Staley can't go out on the floor and play for her team.

545
00:28:31.020 --> 00:28:33.000
She can't be the point guard.

546
00:28:33.120 --> 00:28:35.780
She can't put on a jersey and run the show.

547
00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:41.900
And I question effort in an Elite Eight game.

548
00:28:42.540 --> 00:28:48.800
Duke was getting every 50-50 ball, every loose ball, every offensive rebound, flying in.

549
00:28:48.880 --> 00:28:50.580
Toby Fournier played amazing.

550
00:28:50.980 --> 00:28:51.800
18 points.

551
00:28:52.320 --> 00:28:54.180
Ashlyn Jackson had 13 points.

552
00:28:55.100 --> 00:28:59.740
It was, you know, we talk about the halftime speeches being goaded.

553
00:28:59.740 --> 00:29:06.180
It can't take a halftime speech at this point to light that fire again.

554
00:29:06.540 --> 00:29:10.700
And this game specifically, I didn't see that third quarter South Carolina team.

555
00:29:10.900 --> 00:29:16.840
Like, it wasn't this miraculous turnaround that we were kind of all expecting because they have slow starts.

556
00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:18.560
So, I don't know.

557
00:29:18.780 --> 00:29:27.040
I want this little break before this next game that they really, really realize that they are a great team.

558
00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:29.120
That they can beat teaMs.

559
00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:31.740
But it starts with themselves.

560
00:29:31.780 --> 00:29:35.460
And it has to start the game that way.

561
00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:40.280
I think as we are getting to the Final Four, they have played really good teaMs.

562
00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:41.840
And they barely inched it out.

563
00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:45.740
Now they are going to play a great team in Texas.

564
00:29:45.740 --> 00:29:50.180
And they are going to play a great team in either UCLA or UConn.

565
00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:56.220
And those little mistakes or those second effort plays, it is going to come down to that.

566
00:29:56.220 --> 00:30:01.880
So, South Carolina, I plead you to be the team that we know that you are.

567
00:30:02.720 --> 00:30:05.160
And that starts from within.

568
00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:08.340
It can't always come from your head coach.

569
00:30:08.340 --> 00:30:08.760
Great point.

570
00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:10.420
That's an amazing point.

571
00:30:10.620 --> 00:30:13.400
And to your point, teams are coming in hungry.

572
00:30:13.660 --> 00:30:17.440
We talked about, oh, since 2003, this is the last time.

573
00:30:17.580 --> 00:30:19.020
First time in program history.

574
00:30:19.020 --> 00:30:21.360
These teams are coming in here.

575
00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:25.260
And South Carolina has been here for a fifth year straight.

576
00:30:25.700 --> 00:30:29.580
Teams are coming in hungry, starving for this moment.

577
00:30:29.780 --> 00:30:33.260
And when you look at Texas, they've already battled them three times.

578
00:30:33.260 --> 00:30:34.460
We're going to get this a fourth time.

579
00:30:35.040 --> 00:30:36.580
They've cracked the code once.

580
00:30:36.700 --> 00:30:40.720
It is hard playing a team multiple times because they have you figured it out.

581
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:46.800
And then on the other side, either UCLA and UConn, they both have wins over South Carolina.

582
00:30:47.020 --> 00:30:50.020
Everyone in this Final Four has a win over South Carolina.

583
00:30:50.320 --> 00:30:56.120
And now you're facing them possibly again if you get past Texas and then have to face either or.

584
00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:58.400
You have that scouting report.

585
00:30:58.520 --> 00:30:59.640
You know what needs to be done.

586
00:30:59.740 --> 00:31:01.400
It could get sticky.

587
00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:02.720
That is a great point.

588
00:31:02.720 --> 00:31:04.020
I didn't even realize that.

589
00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:05.800
That's probably their worst nightmare.

590
00:31:05.820 --> 00:31:07.220
They only have three losses, right?

591
00:31:07.420 --> 00:31:08.020
On the season.

592
00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:09.260
Is that correct?

593
00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:11.720
And it's to all these teaMs.

594
00:31:11.980 --> 00:31:12.180
Yes.

595
00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:13.280
Yeah.

596
00:31:13.940 --> 00:31:15.960
I mean, talk about a storyline.

597
00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:17.260
That makes it interesting.

598
00:31:17.740 --> 00:31:18.020
Give me all of it.

599
00:31:18.080 --> 00:31:18.500
I need it.

600
00:31:19.300 --> 00:31:20.620
Oh, let's go.

601
00:31:20.780 --> 00:31:24.360
OK, well, moving on from Duke, had a great season.

602
00:31:24.740 --> 00:31:26.440
The Kara era is live and well.

603
00:31:26.600 --> 00:31:28.140
They have a lot to be proud of.

604
00:31:28.560 --> 00:31:31.320
Again, it really came down to just those final minutes.

605
00:31:31.320 --> 00:31:34.640
They were almost there to upsetting South Carolina.

606
00:31:34.860 --> 00:31:35.920
But they'll clean those up.

607
00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:42.740
I do think coming into next season, there's a couple of names in the portal that are offensive threats.

608
00:31:43.080 --> 00:31:48.260
They need to get an offensive threat who loves to play defense as well.

609
00:31:48.260 --> 00:31:50.220
And that player is out there.

610
00:31:50.260 --> 00:31:56.040
And I think that is that one piece that Duke is missing to put them over the edge.

611
00:31:56.160 --> 00:32:04.800
But to be able to win an elite eight game for South Carolina at 54 points is absolutely insane.

612
00:32:04.800 --> 00:32:08.200
And that was their lowest point scored all season.

613
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:11.280
So that's what Duke defense does to you.

614
00:32:11.720 --> 00:32:11.980
All right.

615
00:32:13.320 --> 00:32:14.520
Texas, TCU.

616
00:32:15.420 --> 00:32:16.380
Holy crap.

617
00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:17.660
The Battle of Texas.

618
00:32:17.720 --> 00:32:20.040
That was so much fun.

619
00:32:20.200 --> 00:32:22.000
I knew that this was going to be fun.

620
00:32:22.240 --> 00:32:23.560
We talk about defense.

621
00:32:23.860 --> 00:32:25.680
Texas, all defense.

622
00:32:26.040 --> 00:32:27.840
TCU, all offense.

623
00:32:28.060 --> 00:32:29.780
Led by Haley Van Litt.

624
00:32:30.260 --> 00:32:32.940
And then Texas led by Madison Booker and Rory Harmon.

625
00:32:33.700 --> 00:32:35.240
But Texas came out on top.

626
00:32:35.240 --> 00:32:37.680
They said, it's all about the burnt orange.

627
00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:38.780
Hook them.

628
00:32:39.480 --> 00:32:43.420
58 to 47 in their elite eight matchup.

629
00:32:43.540 --> 00:32:49.340
This is the first time, like you mentioned, Autumn, Texas is going to the final four since 2003.

630
00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:53.060
Maddie Booker balled out 18 points.

631
00:32:53.480 --> 00:32:55.880
14 of them were in the second half.

632
00:32:56.300 --> 00:33:01.120
Rory Harmon, to me, was the star because she doesn't typically score as heavy.

633
00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:05.200
But she was like, I'm calling my number today.

634
00:33:05.620 --> 00:33:07.040
And 13 points.

635
00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:09.360
11 of those were in the first half.

636
00:33:09.880 --> 00:33:18.320
So what stood out to you from this Texas team saying, we are the inferior Texas score?

637
00:33:18.320 --> 00:33:22.100
Well, you knew coming in, Texas was going to hang its hat on defense.

638
00:33:22.520 --> 00:33:25.260
And TCU is a great offensive team.

639
00:33:25.340 --> 00:33:25.960
And not just great.

640
00:33:25.960 --> 00:33:31.460
They're super efficient when I think of, you know, in terms of scoring inside and out.

641
00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:32.460
They got three ball.

642
00:33:32.600 --> 00:33:34.340
They can work off ball screen actions.

643
00:33:34.400 --> 00:33:36.400
Like, they are constantly moving.

644
00:33:36.400 --> 00:33:40.920
And you have to be on your P's and Q's when you're facing them.

645
00:33:40.980 --> 00:33:42.800
And that's exactly what Texas did.

646
00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:43.920
They looked uncomfortable.

647
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:45.100
They looked sped up.

648
00:33:45.240 --> 00:33:50.820
They looked, in times, were like in discomfort for a full course of 40 minutes that they really

649
00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:52.160
couldn't get anything going.

650
00:33:52.160 --> 00:33:55.560
You know, Madison Booker shining as she always does.

651
00:33:55.820 --> 00:33:56.860
Rory Harmon as well.

652
00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:58.720
These two together are a nightmare.

653
00:33:59.020 --> 00:34:03.160
But honestly, I thought the unsung hero, too, was Kylo Odefer, too.

654
00:34:03.380 --> 00:34:06.480
Like, she came in and did what needed to be done inside.

655
00:34:06.640 --> 00:34:12.400
She had some impressive, game-changing moments, some energy plays as well.

656
00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:15.520
Just Hank, like, just really holding down the paint.

657
00:34:15.700 --> 00:34:20.240
So I love the effort on all ends, both ends, for this Texas team.

658
00:34:20.240 --> 00:34:24.140
And it took them a minute to get going for TCU.

659
00:34:24.320 --> 00:34:27.420
And in an Elite Eight game, like, you can't have that.

660
00:34:27.620 --> 00:34:31.700
But they were, like, they should be proud of what they were able to do and stay close

661
00:34:31.700 --> 00:34:32.200
with them.

662
00:34:32.500 --> 00:34:36.380
With Sedona Prince, obviously, with foul trouble, she ended with, like, four points.

663
00:34:36.380 --> 00:34:39.260
That hurts you because that's a main piece of your big three.

664
00:34:39.480 --> 00:34:41.740
But credit to the Longhorns' defense.

665
00:34:41.980 --> 00:34:43.800
Like, that was true Texas fight.

666
00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:48.940
And it was really cool to see how, you know, a lot of people, including myself, was saying,

667
00:34:49.120 --> 00:34:52.700
like, I'm going to put that out there because it's on the record.

668
00:34:52.920 --> 00:34:53.880
Like, I would say that, too.

669
00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.160
Like, it's on the record.

670
00:34:55.320 --> 00:34:55.600
I mean, come on.

671
00:34:55.640 --> 00:34:56.180
Let's be real.

672
00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:57.080
Like, a lot of people.

673
00:34:57.080 --> 00:34:58.440
You weren't thinking it.

674
00:34:58.500 --> 00:35:00.200
You weren't thinking they were going to make it this far.

675
00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:02.660
And they said, we're winning this for Autumn Johnson.

676
00:35:03.120 --> 00:35:03.240
Only because.

677
00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:05.300
No, I'll take it.

678
00:35:05.300 --> 00:35:12.100
Because the only reason I said that is because I'm like, hey, you know, I want to see if they

679
00:35:12.100 --> 00:35:16.000
can get some threes to go to, like, you know, that outside shot a little bit more.

680
00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:17.860
They get to the rim constantly.

681
00:35:17.860 --> 00:35:19.120
They get in the mid-range.

682
00:35:19.320 --> 00:35:20.920
But will that be enough?

683
00:35:21.340 --> 00:35:24.520
They say, yeah, because teams still have to score on us.

684
00:35:24.860 --> 00:35:26.140
Like, yes.

685
00:35:26.480 --> 00:35:27.000
Curge you.

686
00:35:27.320 --> 00:35:28.700
Big Schaefer, a legend.

687
00:35:28.700 --> 00:35:34.400
And truthfully, honestly, if they can hang their hat on defense and make teams, like,

688
00:35:34.520 --> 00:35:38.040
just search for offense like that, they're a problem.

689
00:35:38.300 --> 00:35:39.200
They've been a problem.

690
00:35:39.200 --> 00:35:42.260
And they've constantly shown us that game after game.

691
00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:43.280
So funny.

692
00:35:43.440 --> 00:35:48.180
I love how you've been doing the threes because they went two for three from the three.

693
00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:49.040
They don't shoot three.

694
00:35:49.200 --> 00:35:51.480
Meanwhile, they don't shoot threes.

695
00:35:51.560 --> 00:35:56.740
They only make three a game as a team, which is just unheard of, especially in this day

696
00:35:56.740 --> 00:35:57.720
and age of basketball.

697
00:35:57.720 --> 00:36:06.240
Also, a stat that jumps out to me from this box score, 21 to 8, and that is turnovers.

698
00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:11.140
TCU turned the ball over 21 times.

699
00:36:11.380 --> 00:36:16.480
A lot of that was in that first quarter to first half where they were getting five-second

700
00:36:16.480 --> 00:36:21.120
violations, half-court, shot clock violations, throwing the ball out of bounds.

701
00:36:21.280 --> 00:36:25.040
It was, I'm uncomfy with this pressure.

702
00:36:25.380 --> 00:36:27.320
Like, please back away.

703
00:36:27.320 --> 00:36:30.340
And Texas was like, no, we're not.

704
00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:31.380
We're going to keep coming.

705
00:36:31.680 --> 00:36:36.680
That was a fun matchup to watch and talk about stories.

706
00:36:36.820 --> 00:36:39.900
TCU is such an incredible story.

707
00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:46.440
For those who don't know, TCU was, they needed tryouts, open tryouts last year.

708
00:36:46.440 --> 00:36:50.480
And the year before that, they were 1-17 in conference.

709
00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:55.080
Just an incredible story for them to be at this level.

710
00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:58.660
And Haley Van Liff to take another team to the Elite Eight.

711
00:36:59.260 --> 00:37:00.280
We wanted that.

712
00:37:00.460 --> 00:37:05.580
I did come around to it like, okay, this would be kind of cool if they went to the Final Four

713
00:37:05.580 --> 00:37:09.900
because this is an unexpected group to get this far.

714
00:37:09.900 --> 00:37:12.280
But Texas was like, no, no, no, no, no.

715
00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:14.620
It's our time to go to the Final Four.

716
00:37:14.620 --> 00:37:15.680
So we're going to take that.

717
00:37:15.920 --> 00:37:18.700
I did want to go back one game real quick.

718
00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:24.200
And how TCU even got to this point is that they beat Notre Dame.

719
00:37:24.400 --> 00:37:27.900
And when I say beat, they beat them.

720
00:37:28.620 --> 00:37:30.660
Notre Dame played terrible.

721
00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:33.660
I think we all watched that.

722
00:37:34.020 --> 00:37:39.840
They did not shoot the ball well, around 31% from the field, if I believe.

723
00:37:40.220 --> 00:37:47.100
The only other team that held Notre Dame to under 37% prior to that was TCU.

724
00:37:47.660 --> 00:37:51.740
So I thought, because I also picked Notre Dame to win that game.

725
00:37:51.920 --> 00:37:57.600
I thought it was going to be this, rah, rah, they beat us earlier in the season, but we're

726
00:37:57.600 --> 00:37:58.280
better now.

727
00:37:58.280 --> 00:38:02.400
And then they proved that they were not better, actually, in this moment.

728
00:38:02.780 --> 00:38:05.420
And TCU just won that game.

729
00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:07.500
Haley Van Liff went off for 26 points.

730
00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:10.440
But we got to say bye-bye to Notre Dame.

731
00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:12.720
And we didn't expect to so soon.

732
00:38:12.840 --> 00:38:13.560
We all picked it.

733
00:38:13.700 --> 00:38:14.200
We did.

734
00:38:14.460 --> 00:38:18.480
I mean, it was that back-to-back loss experience in the beginning of the season.

735
00:38:18.480 --> 00:38:20.200
We're like, oh, it's the Cayman Islands.

736
00:38:20.420 --> 00:38:21.980
Like, it's behind them.

737
00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:25.860
And they went on, I think it was like a 19-game winning streak.

738
00:38:25.880 --> 00:38:26.920
So I was like, okay, cool.

739
00:38:26.920 --> 00:38:30.060
Like, this is a different team that stumbled down the end.

740
00:38:30.200 --> 00:38:33.220
They're going to get it together with this break coming into the NCAA tournament.

741
00:38:34.220 --> 00:38:36.320
TCU said, no, this is our year.

742
00:38:36.420 --> 00:38:37.020
We're going to ride it.

743
00:38:37.160 --> 00:38:38.160
We're the dark horse here.

744
00:38:38.360 --> 00:38:40.200
And just shout out to that program.

745
00:38:40.300 --> 00:38:41.940
Like you said, just turning things around.

746
00:38:41.940 --> 00:38:43.500
It was a historic season.

747
00:38:43.780 --> 00:38:45.880
You know, you look at all the starters.

748
00:38:45.880 --> 00:38:47.520
They had, like, what?

749
00:38:47.700 --> 00:38:50.660
It was like 21 seasons at 12 different schools combined.

750
00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:52.480
It was their first season together.

751
00:38:52.480 --> 00:38:55.580
It was the greatest turnaround that we have seen.

752
00:38:55.820 --> 00:39:00.460
They were 26 wins better than, you know, when Mark Campbell took it over two years ago.

753
00:39:00.720 --> 00:39:02.380
And you're here at the Elite Eight.

754
00:39:02.700 --> 00:39:04.980
Like, you can't ask for anything better.

755
00:39:05.220 --> 00:39:11.140
And just shout out to Haley Van Litt for being so vulnerable throughout this entire journey,

756
00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:12.380
sharing her story.

757
00:39:12.380 --> 00:39:16.380
Because the internet and social media was not nice to her.

758
00:39:16.500 --> 00:39:17.780
Like, let's be so for real.

759
00:39:17.980 --> 00:39:20.220
And at the end of the day, she is a human.

760
00:39:20.460 --> 00:39:23.080
At the end of the day, yes, this is basketball.

761
00:39:23.340 --> 00:39:28.740
But, like, these are 18 to 22-year-old women, young women.

762
00:39:28.980 --> 00:39:34.260
And I'm just so proud of her, of how she's been able to just rewrite her story.

763
00:39:34.260 --> 00:39:35.540
It is not done yet.

764
00:39:35.540 --> 00:39:40.740
It's been so cool to see, like, you know, who she is as a person and how she leans on

765
00:39:40.740 --> 00:39:45.200
her faith and how TCU just poured into her.

766
00:39:45.440 --> 00:39:48.040
Like, she was the perfect piece at the right time.

767
00:39:48.080 --> 00:39:50.740
And I'm so glad that she got to experience that.

768
00:39:50.940 --> 00:39:51.400
For sure.

769
00:39:51.660 --> 00:39:53.900
Such a great story for Haley Van Litt.

770
00:39:54.100 --> 00:39:57.580
And on the other side of that coin, though, for Notre Dame,

771
00:39:59.760 --> 00:40:03.320
rough, rough shooting night for their superstars.

772
00:40:03.320 --> 00:40:09.760
Hannah Hidalgo, Sonia Citron, Olivia Miles, I would say, is their big three.

773
00:40:10.220 --> 00:40:13.920
They go 10 for 44 from the field.

774
00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:18.340
You're not going to win a lot of games like that.

775
00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:20.660
I think it was shot selection.

776
00:40:21.060 --> 00:40:23.800
I think it was lack of ball movement.

777
00:40:24.240 --> 00:40:29.320
It just didn't, it wasn't the Notre Dame that at one point was the best team in the country.

778
00:40:29.320 --> 00:40:31.000
So it was disappointing.

779
00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:37.420
I do think that season as a whole, for them not being in the Final Four, not being in the

780
00:40:37.420 --> 00:40:42.480
championship game, is an underperformance for that whole team.

781
00:40:43.720 --> 00:40:47.480
And Olivia Miles had a decision to make.

782
00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:52.080
You know, she was number two projected pick in the WNBA draft.

783
00:40:52.660 --> 00:40:56.960
Seattle Storm could be heard crying if you really listen.

784
00:40:56.960 --> 00:41:02.760
Because they were, they traded, they were like, yes, this is our player.

785
00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:09.400
And Olivia Miles said, no, I'm not only not coming to the WNBA,

786
00:41:09.700 --> 00:41:13.620
but I am entering the transfer portal.

787
00:41:14.560 --> 00:41:16.480
Autumn, where were you when this news broke?

788
00:41:16.740 --> 00:41:23.680
Because I know that I screenshotted this so fast and sent it to my husband with red sirens,

789
00:41:23.680 --> 00:41:26.420
like 20 red sirens, like, did you see this?

790
00:41:26.560 --> 00:41:28.440
I can't even send this as a DM.

791
00:41:28.680 --> 00:41:31.340
I am texting this to you because what?

792
00:41:31.880 --> 00:41:33.800
I was shook, shook.

793
00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:36.320
I was on the plane, so I couldn't scream.

794
00:41:36.640 --> 00:41:42.360
Thankfully, I had my Wi-Fi turned on because I wouldn't have gotten it until I got off the

795
00:41:42.360 --> 00:41:42.680
plane.

796
00:41:42.860 --> 00:41:44.300
So I was locked in.

797
00:41:44.440 --> 00:41:50.540
You know, when it dropped down, it was like, oh, she foregoed her WNBA draft,

798
00:41:50.540 --> 00:41:51.480
that part.

799
00:41:51.660 --> 00:41:52.460
And I'm like, okay, cool.

800
00:41:52.600 --> 00:41:54.260
Like, like, she's going to come back for another year.

801
00:41:54.360 --> 00:41:56.440
And I saw a transfer portal.

802
00:41:56.740 --> 00:41:58.160
I wanted to scream.

803
00:41:58.340 --> 00:41:59.980
I was like, what?

804
00:42:00.320 --> 00:42:02.760
I think that's the part that's so shocking.

805
00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:03.540
Like, okay, cool.

806
00:42:03.660 --> 00:42:04.640
Like, she wants to come back.

807
00:42:04.840 --> 00:42:07.080
Didn't end off on the note that she wanted to.

808
00:42:07.440 --> 00:42:10.580
Has the perfect pieces around her for a championship run.

809
00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:14.360
Neil Ivey is like an iconic coach that has turned,

810
00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:18.280
just kept the ball rolling after the Muffin McGraw era.

811
00:42:19.240 --> 00:42:20.560
This team has everything.

812
00:42:20.720 --> 00:42:21.520
And it's Notre Dame.

813
00:42:21.740 --> 00:42:23.240
Like, she has started there.

814
00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:27.260
You look at players and it's like, okay, they're going to start and finish there.

815
00:42:27.400 --> 00:42:28.960
They are Notre Dame through and through.

816
00:42:29.700 --> 00:42:32.480
But this one shook me because of that reason.

817
00:42:32.700 --> 00:42:34.520
Like, I thought she was going to start and finish there.

818
00:42:34.740 --> 00:42:38.880
And just with everything around her, she was going to end her final chapter there.

819
00:42:38.980 --> 00:42:40.240
So that's why it shook me.

820
00:42:41.020 --> 00:42:41.460
Crazy.

821
00:42:42.420 --> 00:42:42.860
Wild.

822
00:42:43.780 --> 00:42:50.320
Last thing I'll say on this before we move on is, you know, we were all excited coming

823
00:42:50.320 --> 00:42:56.140
into this season on how Hannah Hidalgo and Olivia Miles were going to play with each other.

824
00:42:56.560 --> 00:43:04.880
And I think a lot of people forget that it was Olivia Miles' team by herself before.

825
00:43:05.280 --> 00:43:06.940
And then she got injured.

826
00:43:07.120 --> 00:43:10.900
And then it was Hannah Hidalgo's team by herself for a season.

827
00:43:10.900 --> 00:43:13.580
And then it was like, yay, we're coming together.

828
00:43:13.580 --> 00:43:14.520
We're going to see this.

829
00:43:14.640 --> 00:43:15.620
And they're so young.

830
00:43:15.620 --> 00:43:17.980
So we could possibly see this for multiple years.

831
00:43:18.560 --> 00:43:19.480
I don't know.

832
00:43:19.620 --> 00:43:20.320
I don't want to speculate.

833
00:43:20.320 --> 00:43:21.260
I have no idea.

834
00:43:21.520 --> 00:43:25.280
I don't have any reports of what's going on behind the scenes.

835
00:43:25.500 --> 00:43:27.040
It could be personal.

836
00:43:27.080 --> 00:43:28.020
It could not be.

837
00:43:28.220 --> 00:43:30.860
It could be that there's not enough basketballs.

838
00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:31.980
It could not be.

839
00:43:31.980 --> 00:43:36.400
I just know that both of those players are really, really good.

840
00:43:36.780 --> 00:43:40.360
And we got to see it shake out together.

841
00:43:40.580 --> 00:43:45.720
But now what excites me is that this is going to continue this parody conversation.

842
00:43:45.720 --> 00:43:50.640
And that now it's not this front-loaded, you know, backcourt on one team.

843
00:43:50.860 --> 00:43:54.800
But now Olivia Miles is going to go to another team and immediately make them better.

844
00:43:55.100 --> 00:43:59.780
Or she's going to go to another team and she is going to be the superstar all on her own.

845
00:43:59.780 --> 00:44:01.580
But we know what she can do.

846
00:44:01.600 --> 00:44:04.800
So it's not like she's going somewhere else to prove anything.

847
00:44:05.100 --> 00:44:06.680
We already know that she's a baller.

848
00:44:06.860 --> 00:44:10.260
She just maybe has one other year and wants to see what's out there.

849
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:15.580
And she'll still be a top pick for the WNBA next year.

850
00:44:15.860 --> 00:44:16.340
Absolutely.

851
00:44:17.100 --> 00:44:17.580
Absolutely.

852
00:44:17.920 --> 00:44:22.200
Can't wait to when we get on with these microphones and when she announces where she goes,

853
00:44:22.380 --> 00:44:24.920
which, by the way, is happening very quickly.

854
00:44:25.160 --> 00:44:27.820
They are entering the portal and they're making decisions.

855
00:44:27.820 --> 00:44:29.640
And I have no idea where she's going.

856
00:44:29.780 --> 00:44:32.600
They're like, I'm trying to think, OK, where would she go?

857
00:44:32.600 --> 00:44:33.580
And I don't know.

858
00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:35.160
I'm like, who needs a point guard?

859
00:44:35.160 --> 00:44:35.740
Would I go for those living miles?

860
00:44:36.100 --> 00:44:36.620
NIL.

861
00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:37.820
There's so much.

862
00:44:38.240 --> 00:44:39.120
I have no idea.

863
00:44:39.360 --> 00:44:39.520
OK.

864
00:44:40.120 --> 00:44:47.740
Last one of the roundups, real quick, because it was pretty quickly and obvious.

865
00:44:48.440 --> 00:44:54.320
UConn, as a number two seed, playing against a USC team, who was a number one seed.

866
00:44:54.320 --> 00:45:00.460
But like we mentioned before, Juju Watkins, their superstar, goes down with an ACL injury

867
00:45:00.460 --> 00:45:01.660
in the round of 32.

868
00:45:02.140 --> 00:45:08.900
So this was a USC team that had to kind of make the impossible happen and go up against

869
00:45:08.900 --> 00:45:15.060
not just any team, but a UConn team that is playing really, really well, firing on all

870
00:45:15.060 --> 00:45:20.540
cylinders with a Paige Beckers who's playing out of her brain right now.

871
00:45:20.540 --> 00:45:31.400
So UConn ends up winning 78 to 64 over USC, and they advance to their 24th final four.

872
00:45:31.640 --> 00:45:34.960
So we're talking about other teams where, oh, it's been so long.

873
00:45:35.660 --> 00:45:37.140
UConn is like, yeah, yeah, yeah.

874
00:45:37.320 --> 00:45:38.420
This is the standard.

875
00:45:38.740 --> 00:45:40.080
Actually, this isn't even the standard.

876
00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:44.820
This is just one step to go to the championship, which is the standard for us.

877
00:45:45.140 --> 00:45:52.520
But Paige Beckers, whoo, you are a baller.

878
00:45:52.820 --> 00:45:56.100
31 points, 9 of 18 shooting for this time.

879
00:45:56.340 --> 00:46:01.900
She had a 40 piece the game before that and another 30 piece the game before that.

880
00:46:02.080 --> 00:46:06.520
The last player to have three games in a row with 30 points.

881
00:46:06.700 --> 00:46:07.400
Do you know who it was?

882
00:46:07.500 --> 00:46:08.580
Paige Beckers herself.

883
00:46:08.580 --> 00:46:10.820
Yes, she's her.

884
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:12.180
Her freshman season.

885
00:46:12.680 --> 00:46:14.280
Like, come on.

886
00:46:14.620 --> 00:46:16.480
So we know what Paige can do.

887
00:46:16.720 --> 00:46:18.100
She is so, so good.

888
00:46:18.300 --> 00:46:25.840
But Autumn, I also want you to talk about Sarah Strong and how the freshmen came into this game

889
00:46:25.840 --> 00:46:30.380
knowing that she did not have great outings the games before.

890
00:46:30.720 --> 00:46:32.660
But this is her first tournament.

891
00:46:32.660 --> 00:46:34.600
She was in high school last year.

892
00:46:34.780 --> 00:46:36.460
People forget she's only a freshman.

893
00:46:36.460 --> 00:46:40.920
How does she just turn the gas all the way up in this?

894
00:46:41.040 --> 00:46:46.520
Not only that, but to have that mindship and confidence knowing that you're going up against

895
00:46:46.520 --> 00:46:52.880
a lottery pick in Kiki Area Finn, too, to battle against her and still have that same dominant

896
00:46:52.880 --> 00:46:55.760
performance is unheard of for a freshman.

897
00:46:56.020 --> 00:47:01.880
And Sarah Strong continuously, night in and night out, provides such a consistent effort

898
00:47:01.880 --> 00:47:03.960
that just has you in awe.

899
00:47:04.220 --> 00:47:05.520
Like, we're like, wait a minute.

900
00:47:05.700 --> 00:47:07.420
In another life, is she a freshman?

901
00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:09.220
Like, what?

902
00:47:09.460 --> 00:47:10.920
This girl is special.

903
00:47:10.920 --> 00:47:14.960
And you see, you know, her parents and everything where she came from.

904
00:47:15.100 --> 00:47:17.780
Like, obviously, that's been built in her.

905
00:47:17.780 --> 00:47:21.040
It's in her DNA, but she's going to be something special.

906
00:47:21.240 --> 00:47:23.080
Yes, Paige Beckers is about to leave.

907
00:47:23.220 --> 00:47:27.080
But you have Sarah Strong, who is coming in, knocking in, knocking down threes.

908
00:47:27.460 --> 00:47:28.600
She's so versatile.

909
00:47:28.600 --> 00:47:33.380
Like, the spin move she had, just the composure, the body control.

910
00:47:33.580 --> 00:47:39.860
Like, she is one of one, and she does everything, like, just like the little things that sometimes

911
00:47:39.860 --> 00:47:42.400
don't even show up in the box score as well.

912
00:47:42.520 --> 00:47:49.160
Her efficiency, her consistency, her ability to, like, work off the dribble, her footwork.

913
00:47:49.440 --> 00:47:53.440
It's unmatched, and it's just going to be really exciting to see that, okay, this was

914
00:47:53.440 --> 00:47:54.240
your freshman year.

915
00:47:54.480 --> 00:47:56.940
How do you keep growing from here?

916
00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:57.860
Because that's scary.

917
00:47:57.860 --> 00:47:59.580
That is scary.

918
00:48:00.160 --> 00:48:06.080
She finished with 22 points and 17 rebounds plus four assists.

919
00:48:06.520 --> 00:48:08.140
For those that don't know, that's really good.

920
00:48:08.440 --> 00:48:12.020
Those are really good stats, especially as a freshman.

921
00:48:12.040 --> 00:48:16.280
Right, people have been comparing her to Maya Moore, and I see it.

922
00:48:16.420 --> 00:48:17.780
And that's a great comparison.

923
00:48:18.020 --> 00:48:22.380
That's a lot to live up to, but she's creating her own paths.

924
00:48:22.540 --> 00:48:23.660
She's playing her own game.

925
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:27.460
She can do so many different things at 6'1".

926
00:48:27.460 --> 00:48:31.440
Like, as an undersized post, again, I need tomorrow.

927
00:48:31.780 --> 00:48:32.440
It doesn't matter.

928
00:48:32.600 --> 00:48:34.040
Like, that's just built in you.

929
00:48:36.890 --> 00:48:40.450
Man, to just be in the same sentence as Maya Moore.

930
00:48:40.630 --> 00:48:44.710
Like, I'm trying to think what sentence I would be in as Maya Moore.

931
00:48:44.710 --> 00:48:47.210
I think only if we were in the same room.

932
00:48:47.430 --> 00:48:47.630
Yeah, yeah.

933
00:48:47.650 --> 00:48:48.430
Like, okay, yeah.

934
00:48:48.630 --> 00:48:49.550
Who's all in this room?

935
00:48:49.670 --> 00:48:51.690
Oh, Jordan Robinson and Maya Moore.

936
00:48:51.950 --> 00:48:52.550
Literally, that's it.

937
00:48:52.710 --> 00:48:54.990
And they probably wouldn't even be next to each other.

938
00:48:54.990 --> 00:49:00.170
And our names wouldn't even be next to each other in a sentence like that.

939
00:49:00.810 --> 00:49:07.950
So for Sarah Strong to be compared, I think it's because of her versatility and her efficiency.

940
00:49:08.190 --> 00:49:14.830
Maya Moore was a player who could get a bucket at any single spot on the floor and is a forward,

941
00:49:14.850 --> 00:49:16.410
but also has guard skills.

942
00:49:16.550 --> 00:49:19.910
You see her bringing the ball up, but then she could also post you up.

943
00:49:19.910 --> 00:49:21.130
And it doesn't matter.

944
00:49:21.350 --> 00:49:22.990
She can score at any level.

945
00:49:23.210 --> 00:49:28.410
So UConn, you are always spoiled and have a plethora of riches.

946
00:49:28.410 --> 00:49:34.270
And now I am so jealous that you get Sarah Strong in a UConn uniform for three more seasons,

947
00:49:34.390 --> 00:49:36.770
regardless of what happens this weekend.

948
00:49:36.770 --> 00:49:40.010
She is still going to be able to fall out for you.

949
00:49:40.210 --> 00:49:43.850
Real quick on USC, they tried their hardeSt.

950
00:49:44.190 --> 00:49:49.730
It was going to be a huge load on freshmen, like we talked about, maybe.

951
00:49:49.910 --> 00:49:53.050
In UConn's case, that was okay because the freshmen turned up.

952
00:49:53.370 --> 00:50:00.110
But freshmen who were used to playing the backseat to a Juju Watkins and a Kiki Area fan all season long

953
00:50:00.110 --> 00:50:01.870
were asked to do a lot.

954
00:50:01.870 --> 00:50:03.970
And it was a very, very heavy task.

955
00:50:04.050 --> 00:50:05.390
But it was actually the senior.

956
00:50:05.610 --> 00:50:08.830
It was Rhea Marshall who had such a great game for the Trojans.

957
00:50:08.990 --> 00:50:12.350
23 points, 14 rebounds, 7 for 12 shooting.

958
00:50:12.650 --> 00:50:16.570
One of her best games of her career comes in her last game of her career.

959
00:50:16.570 --> 00:50:19.410
So super proud for Rhea Marshall.

960
00:50:19.770 --> 00:50:22.890
And this USC team has to be very, very proud.

961
00:50:23.070 --> 00:50:27.050
Juju sent a message on Instagram saying she wished she was in the building.

962
00:50:27.350 --> 00:50:29.270
She is so proud of her team.

963
00:50:29.730 --> 00:50:30.630
Just heartbreaking.

964
00:50:30.730 --> 00:50:33.770
But I know that this is not the end of their story.

965
00:50:33.930 --> 00:50:36.590
Like they have really solid pieces to get them back here.

966
00:50:36.590 --> 00:50:39.790
Yes, they had the number one freshman class come in.

967
00:50:40.070 --> 00:50:45.810
This is now the place to be that Juju has kind of like, not even kind of, she has just

968
00:50:45.810 --> 00:50:47.490
rejuvenized this program.

969
00:50:47.710 --> 00:50:51.750
And, you know, what she was able to do in her freshman year carried over to her sophomore

970
00:50:51.750 --> 00:50:52.070
year.

971
00:50:52.210 --> 00:50:56.470
Just praying that she comes back stronger and healthier than ever, which she will.

